ution that moves discussion forward. Perhaps we can say we agree with Emily on B but note that Candidate C's 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere is strong, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be concerning. Or we could ask a question to James or Emily for more info. But we can also just present our view.\n\nGiven the guidelines, we should reference Emily's point and add our own evidence. We can say we support B but note that Candidate D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but arrogance and weak leadership are concerns. Or we could shift recommendation if we think another candidate is stronger overall.\n\nWe need to decide vote. Likely we will also vote for Candidate B, but we need to give reasons. Or we could propose Candidate C as alternative because reliability and crew atmosphere are crucial. However, C has communication difficulty and egocentric, which may be serious.\n\nGiven the criteria, reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability. Candidate B: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience (handles stress well), technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills), decision quality? Not mentioned. Crew cooperation? Not mentioned, but concerns about pretentiousness and tone. Responsibility? Not mentioned. Adaptability? Not mentioned.\n\nCandidate C: reliability (100% reliable), decision quality (quick correct decisions), crew cooperation (positive atmosphere), but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Stress resilience unknown.\n\nCandidate D: stress resilience (responds adequately), attention (concentrates well), problem solving (extremely well), responsibility (takes seriously), but arrogance, weak leadership, moodiness (uncooperative). Reliability unknown.\n\nCandidate A: anticipation of danger, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but unorganized, not good at criticism, sometimes not good at taking criticism, maybe not reliable.\n\nThus B seems balanced but missing some aspects. C strong reliability and crew atmosphere but communication issues. D strong responsibility and problem solving but arrogance.\n\nWe could argue that B's communication concerns are less severe than C's egocentric and difficulty communicating, and D's arrogance. So B remains best.\n\nThus we will vote Candidate B.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: maybe \"I agree with Emily's provisional recommendation of Candidate B, and here's why...\"\n\nWe should reference specific facts: B is very conscientious (operational reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), excellent computer skills (technical competence). Concern: pretentious, wrong tone (communication). We can note that while these concerns exist, they are addressable.\n\nWe can also note that we still need to discuss other candidates, but B currently leads.\n\nThus produce.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
